{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Which we spoke to you in the land of Egypt.</b> And where did they speak? ״יֵרֶא ה' עֲלֵיכֶם וְיִשְׁפֹּט״ (Exodus 5) (Mekhilta)." "<b>ממתנו.</b> — that we die. And if it had been punctuated with a melafum it would be read as מִמִּיתָתֵנוּ. Now that it is punctuated with a shuruk, it reads: that we die. So too ״מִי יִתֵּן מוּתֵנוּ״ (Exodus 16) — that we die; and so too ״מִי יִתֵּן מוּתִי״ of Absalom (II Samuel 19) — that I die. Like ״לְיוֹם קוּמִי לְעַד״ (Zephaniah 3), ״עַד יוֹם שׁוּבִי בְשָׁלוֹם״ (II Chronicles 18) — that I arise, that I return."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:09.968075604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}